maria: quick heads up — i'm about to land a terraform change to the karpenter provisioner for inference pools. adding a taint (dedicated=inference:NoSchedule) + nodeSelector so noisy batch jobs don't land on these nodes. quick sanity check: will that block HPA/VPA from scaling down nodes? also need to wire a secret for prometheus-adapter credentials. snippet below.

```hcl
resource "karpenter_provisioner" "inference" {
  name = "inference-pool"
  labels = { "pool" = "inference" }
  taints = [{ key = "dedicated", value = "inference", effect = "NoSchedule" }]
  provider { instance_profile = "irsa-inference" }
}
```

jon: cc @chris — from what i remember, taints themselves don't stop HPA from scaling; it's the pod scheduling semantics. Karpenter will only terminate nodes when pods can be moved or are evicted. if your inference deployments tolerate the taint they will stay, so ensure the batch jobs don't tolerate it. also double-check karpenter's ttlAfterEmpty behavior (we set it pretty long for this pool). :eyes:

chris: add tolerations on the inference deployments instead of making pods tolerate by default. for HPA/VPA: HPA scales replicas, not nodes. nodes only scale through Karpenter/CA when pods are pending. VPA mutating is tricky; for deployments we prefer HPA+vertical autoscaler recommendation only. if you need pods to be movable, add `podDisruptionBudget` low enough or ensure graceful termination.

sara: prometheus-adapter needs a secret with read creds for the metrics endpoint if you're using remote prom. we created `prom-adapter-creds` in vault for staging. terraform snippet to wire vault secret -> k8s secret:

```hcl
resource "vault_kv_secret_v2" "prom_creds" { /* vault config */ }
resource "kubernetes_secret" "prom_adapter" {
  metadata { name = "prom-adapter-creds" }
  data = { config = base64encode(vault_kv_secret_v2.prom_creds.data_json) }
}
```

maria: got it — i'll add tolerations to the inference daemonset, make sure batch jobs don't tolerate the taint, set `karpenter.k8s.aws/ttl-after-empty: "10m"` annotation on the provisioner, and wire the vault -> k8s secret. i'll open a PR and mark it WIP. please review the canary in staging before prod apply.

deploy-bot: deploy-bot: staged plan created: `pr/4321` by maria — plan shows no diffs for other provisioners.

maria: thanks all — tagging @jon @chris for review. i'll wait 24h for feedback then roll.

chris: quick note — when you open the PR please include a short test plan (how to simulate pending pods + verify scale down). otherwise lgtm.

maria: will do, thx :thumbsup:
